This is probably the first ascension ever that used the pudding
farming bot, so Art convinced me of posting this YAAP for historical
reasons. ;-)

Starting stats: St:14 Dx:13 Co:12 In:9 Wi:11 Ch:16

Starting inv: spellbook of protection, which IMHO isn't quite as
useful as healing or sleep, and a magic marker (yay).

Dlvl 3 had a huge bookstore, where I bought a spellbook of extra
healing.

Minetown was a bones level from an Archaeologist who seemed to have
tried the protection racket, so I got a sack with lots of useless
dwarvish armor and a touchstone. The altar was non-coaligned. I went
up to the main dungeon again, because lower mines are dangerous.

After digging up a magic memory vault I lost the weaponless conduct
due to the usual pick-axe accident.

Sokoban had the "oR.

After looting some more vaults, I went back to minetown to buy some
protection, and then I dared to go deeper into the mines, where my dog
got poly'ed into a winter wolf. He happily took out the watchmen and
the watch captain, but didn't want to attack the priest yet.

In Mines Dlvl 10 I took out a mind flayer by using the E-word and a
/oMM. At Dlvl 11 I found a BoH! :-)
Minesend was the level-teleport-trap version... annoying.
By now my winter wolf was strong enough to attack the town priest,
but got killed even though i kept casting extra healing on him.

Stat snapshot around turn 10k: St:17 Dx:14 Co:18 In:9 Wi:10 Ch:16

Bigroom was no threat.

At Dlvl 12 a fscking arch-lich made my robe crumble to dust, and
summoned monsters. An ochre jelly engulfed me and brought down my
HP, so I read a scroll of teleportation, which turned out to be
cursed. I tamed a winged gargoyle and went back to minetown, but
he didn't want to attack the priest either. :-(

Went back to the arch-lich and got rid of him by burning E at the
upstairs with a wand of fire and whacking him. Then took out a red
dragon and a MMF (with my trusty /oMM) the arch-lich had summoned.
Then I stepped on the polytrap that had probably created the L.
Luckily there was no robe left to blow, but i just turned into a
housecat anyway. A xan brought me back to human form.

I got lucky and found a [CoMR shortly afterwards.

Dlvl 14 finally had an altar, where I sacced for some Luck and
Giantslayer (yuck). Then I lost vegan by eating a wraith corpse
without thinking. Well... at least I could now eat the royal jelly
from a beehive on Dlvl 16 too. And a tengu to get teleportitis.
Then tried on all my rings - luckily one of them was teleport control.

I sacced some more and got Vorpy at T:23415. With the enchant weapon
scrolls from the bookstore I quickly got it to +7.
Then I wrote some enchant armor scrolls to get to AC:-14.

Dlvl 22 had the portal to Fort Ludios as well as a temple to donate
the $$ to. :-)
One soldier had a /oDeath, which got zapped empty before I got hold
of it. Vorpy decapitated Croesus. His throne let me wish for a pair
of speed boots!

After enchanting and donating some more, i was down to AC:-18...
ready to take on the Castle, which was right below Medusa (Titan
version, but he didn't make any trouble. Perseus had the levboots).
I used a bugle to mastermind the tune, and then let the drawbridge
crush most of the monsters. The WoW was at (0:2). I already knew
the charging scroll, so I wished for a magic marker and a [HoB.
Burned the marker to write a scroll of genocide, which I didn't
know yet, then wished for yet another marker and finally succeeded.
Wiped out L, N and c.

Stat snapshot at turn 30k:
St:18/23 Dx:18 Co:19 In:15 Wi:19 Ch:17
HP:148(148) Pw:102(102) AC:-21 Exp:18

Then I was ready to prepare a pudding farm. I set up a small boulder
fort at the altar with an E square nearby and dug out most of the
level. Didn't bother to light it. Reverse genocided black puddings and
on went the fun, thanks to a stethoscope and the extra healing spell.

After manually getting the farm started, I used blindcoder's bot to
go on farming. I don't think using a bot is more 'cheating' than
pudding farming already is (though i'd rather call it 'abuse of game
features'), because it doesn't make impossible things possible, it
just makes some things easier for the user. Not even faster, because
with a stupid macro that repeatedly attacked puddings I wouldn't
encounter the delay waiting for game output. Because my RTT to nao
(yes, a public server ;) is 200ms, the farming speed was slower than
1 pudding kill per second.
And I couldn't let the bot run unattended because it sometimes hung
while trying to pick up rotten corpses, sometimes it did stupid things
like teleporting me away or moving a boulder, once a rock mole blocked
the entry to my fort, sometimes giants destroyed my fort (even though
I'd engraved E under the boulders, though only with a /oDig at first,
as I didn't know it would erode without anyone stepping on it), and
once a tengu with a wand of digging was generated on my E square,
making a hole in the floor...

But despite those nuisances it took me all in all only about 20 hours
and less than 100k turns of farming to get to AC:-128, get [GoD, a
T-shirt and a magic lamp, all spells and an assortment of scrolls and
potions. No lucky /WoW from farming though. :-(

Stat snapshot after shutting down the farm:
St:18/68 Dx:23 Co:18 In:23 Wi:23 Ch:18 Neutral S:20815408
HP:1822(1822) Pw:149(149) AC:-128 Exp:21 T:105682

Then I started the Quest and the ascension run, which naturally went
on very quickly and smoothly. Zapped sleep on Master Kaen, and he fell
quickly. Heavily relied on magic mapping and detect treasure in
Gehennom. All demon lords/princes except Juiblex were decapitated
by good ole Vorpy, and Juiblex went down fast.
I used conflict on the planes except Astral.
I had the Finger at 14% at the end, and used it 3 times for Rodney,
and 2 times for Famine. Genocided U, H and D on Astral because they
were summoned a lot and annoyed me. At Famine's altar which was Chaotic
I quickly decided not to bother with the rest of Astral, especially with
Pestilence and Death, even though it would probably have been rather
easy with -128 AC and the Finger. So I wizard locked the temple door,
wished for a greased [HoOA, burned 125 points of divine protection,
and offered the Amulet.

The voice of Huan Ti booms: "Congratulations, mortal!"--More--
"In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of Immortality!"--More--
You ascend to the status of Demigod...--More--

